Pseudo-terminals on Radix: /devices/ptmx (/dev is a link to /devices),
and the terminal /devices/pts/N, N from TIOCGPTN, unlocked with
TIOCSPTLCK, as Radix's C library's posix_openpt, ptsname and unlockpt
do. syscall.Syscall fails on Radix, and this module does not require
golang.org/x/sys, so ioctl is package syscall's ioctlPtr, which Radix's
Go gives for linkname. Its pointer is passed as a uintptr, so ioctl is
marked //go:uintptrescapes: what it points to stays alive, and on the
heap, until the call returns.

